{{define "communication"}}
Ordinary progress, milestones and resolved failures go in the ledger. Send one consolidated readiness report when master must schedule review/testing or avoid a mistaken wait. Submissions, evidence and gates already notify the right people: do not also send their summaries. Report terminal outcomes, not polls. Contact master when acceptance changes or a gate must be released. Developers and reviewers consolidate findings directly. Answer actionable requests with message reply; never reply to pure acknowledgments or obsolete task notices. Use judgment, not message quotas: surface real blockers and time-sensitive risks promptly.
{{end}}
